# A1-LN (STOP, the kill signal): Lever N merged with prefix reuse, audited, on the window image: the attach and the exactness shapes (concurrent8_skew and the three levern_equal rows). It runs FIRST after A0X0:
# an attach death shows within about 5 minutes. READ: G-NP0 (install lines: the scheduler, the platform wrap, the route and its warm), G-NP1 (digests equal the control's by tokens_sha), G-NP4 (the route epoch scope),
# the memory ledger after attach (free DRAM above the prefill transient plus a margin), no 'lever N REFUSED' line, no audit mismatch. An attach death on L1 or the trace region is the LEAN swap, on DRAM the POOL swap,
# a G-NP4 failure the EPOCH swap (ORDER.txt, SWAPS): one re-run under a reserve tag; a second failure ends Lever N for the window. Measured basis: an audited attach is 2-5 minutes (v536 120 s, v578 300 s).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-1 window pack (tp4-w1-levern-jobs: Lever N + prefix reuse, exactness; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_skew,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy,levern_equal_long
C2_BOX_MINUTES=165
